      "@type": "bootstrap:Process",
      "depiction": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/assets/img/workflows/classify-and-code-content.svg",
      "description": "Classifies and codes L1 extracted statements (recommendations, implementation practices, remarks, proposed coverage exclusions) and L2 DAK slots (personas, business processes, guideline domains, conditions, interventions, medicines, GRADE ratings), following the terminology-coding methodology and the classify-and-code-content skill. The authoring agent runs terminology-lookup down the four-rung reuse-first ladder, records provenance (declared, context, inferred) and candidate status, and stages the result. A person in the l1-extraction-reviewer lane signs or rejects each exclusion proposed in exclusions.proposed.json against the printed page (sections/page-NNN.md). A person in the terminologist / ontologist lane then adjudicates the candidate codings, SKOS match precision (exactMatch vs closeMatch) and any Rung 4 local glossary candidates.",
      "enforcement": "advisory",
      "flowCount": 13,
      "inSubgraph": "http://smart.who.int/base/directory/smart-base-L1",
